Hi,

At FOSDEM on the 1st and 2nd of February 2014, there will be a graphics=20
DevRoom. URL https://fosdem.org/2014/

The focus of this DevRoom is the same as the X.org DevRooms of yore;=20
anything to do with graphics on open source software goes.

This includes:
* Graphics drivers: from display to media to 3d drivers, both in kernel=20
  or userspace. Be it part of DRM, KMS, (direct)FB, V4L, Xorg, Mesa...
* Input drivers: kernel and userspace.
* Windowing systems: X, Wayland, Mir, directFB, ...
* Even colour management and other areas which i might have overlooked=20
  above are accepted.

Slots are 1 hour long. This partly to avoid confusion and people running=20
all over the place all the time. As a speaker, you do not have to fill=20
your whole hour, smallish gaps are never wasted time.

Slots will be handed out on a first come, first serve basis. The best=20
slots will go to those who apply the soonest. The amount of slots is=20
currently not known yet, but i expect there to be around 16 available (8=20
on each day), so act quickly.

Talk Submission:
----------------

New this year is that speakers are expected to submit proposals to the=20
FOSDEM organizers scheduling system directly (pentabarf). This reduces=20
overhead for all involved (especially me - but this directive came from=20
the FOSDEM team), but holds a few caveats.

The biggest advantage is that you will be able to adjust your own=20
information and your talk information directly. And you can therefor=20
yourself make sure that the information is correct and complete, and you=20
can even make it match the structure of the FOSDEM website. This is a=20
vast improvement over the freeform emails i used to get, which i then=20
had to form up (somewhat) nicely. This does mean that i will end up=20
having to chase people more...

Remember that FOSDEM is not like XDC, it's not some 50 odd people=20
meeting with a sliding schedule which only gets filled in on the last=20
day. Upwards of 7000 people are visiting this event, and most of them=20
get a printed booklet or use the schedule on the FOSDEM website or an=20
app for their phone to figure out what to watch or participate in next.=20
So please put some effort in your talk submission and details.

As for deadlines, i hope to have a pretty much complete schedule between=20
christmas and the new year. The rockhard printed schedule deadline is=20
probably January 10th, after that you will not be featured in the=20
booklet and you will have a lot less visitors. I will find out to what=20
extent i will be able to lock down entries and descriptions during those=20
final days. Don't count on this deadline though. First come first serve,=20
and there are perhaps only 16 slots.

